// REQUIRES: host-linux-amd64, clang
// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/run-cabi.py --flags "%gopp_link_flags" --edges 16 %gopp %t.d 0 1000
// P04.11 (D4.4): the enumerated signatures at the edges of the register
// classes (Inputs/gen-cabi.py --mode edges, c2's set: every struct of one and
// two scalars, of three and four from smaller sets, arrays of every length
// around 8, 16 and 32 bytes, nested structs and arrays of structs, empty
// structs and zero-length arrays, a struct after enough scalars to use the
// integer or vector registers up, two structs in a row, narrow integers and
// bools among wide ones; each as an argument, a
// result and both) against C built by Clang, byte for byte, as
// cabi-amd64.test does for random ones. One in 16 here; all of them in
// cabi-edges-amd64.long.test, on arm64 in cabi-edges-arm64*.test.
